.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
This little helper class constructs a dummy mesh for a given scene the resembles the node hierarchy\&. This is useful for file formats that don't carry any mesh data but only animation data\&. 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "Assimp::SkeletonMeshBuilder::SkeletonMeshBuilder (\fBaiScene\fP * pScene, \fBaiNode\fP * root = \fRnullptr\fP, bool bKnobsOnly = \fRfalse\fP)"
The constructor processes the given scene and adds a mesh there\&.
.PP
Does nothing if the scene already has mesh data\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpScene\fP The scene for which a skeleton mesh should be constructed\&. 
.br
\fIroot\fP The node to start with\&. nullptr is the scene root 
.br
\fIbKnobsOnly\fP Set this to true if you don't want the connectors between the knobs representing the nodes\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBvoid\fP Assimp::SkeletonMeshBuilder::CreateGeometry (const \fBaiNode\fP * pNode)\fR [protected]\fP"
Recursively builds a simple mesh representation for the given node and also creates a joint for the node that affects this part of the mesh\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
